      "reasons": [
        "The packet does not define the neonatal period as “the newborn stage soon after birth”; it only refers to “newborns” and the “neonatal period” in the context of seizures/hypoxia, without giving an explicit definition of the term’s timeframe.",
        "While the packet supports that the neonatal period is “very sensitive in terms of the development of synapses” and links this to memory and learning via synaptic plasticity, the definition’s wording extends this to general “events in this period may affect later learning and memory-related brain processes,” which is not stated as a general rule in the packet (it specifically discusses hypoxia-induced neonatal seizures)."
